{"spec_element": "invariant",
 "proof_obligation": "preservation",
 "diagnosis": "The loop invariant only describes the already-swapped outer regions and says nothing about the untouched middle region i..a.Length-1-i. After a swap, the verifier does not know that a[i] and a[a.Length-1-i] still hold their original values, so it cannot show the newly swapped elements equal old(a[a.Length-1-k]). For odd lengths it also cannot conclude the middle element is unchanged at exit. Adding an invariant that the middle region is unchanged (a[k] == old(a[k])) fixes preservation and the postcondition."}
